[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says "known · one issue, one fix queued". It holds three problems.
Fixing the parser closes one of them. The other two stay broken and keep coming in as "the same bug".

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one fix. Each problem below has its own ticket. Merge new reports by problem, not by subject.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## How to tell them apart

- **Parser:** day and month swap. Every day-first tenant, every channel except the booking-v3 form.
- **Hint:** the same swap, but only through the booking-v3 form (Alder Physio, Copper Studio, Pale Harbour).
  The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, people type month first, and the form reads day first.
  Fixing the parser does not fix this. The hint text does.
- **Shift:** the date moves by one day. A day/month swap can never do that. Look for weekdays one apart,
  "before I booked it", or two cities seeing different days. The desk listed these in its notes and then
  filed them under parser anyway.

## What went wrong in triage

- Merging on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put all three into one ticket,
  because all three get subjects like "Wrong date again".
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It is wrong for many reports in every problem.
  Use the tenant and the channel (`#lib/kb/causes`), not the tag.
- The export repeats some reports. Count by id.

